  "articleBody": "Hiring someone to completely gut and rebuild your bathroom is a major commitment, and asking the right questions upfront saves serious headaches later. Before signing an agreement, you want total clarity on how the contractor manages trade work, scheduling, and unexpected conditions behind the walls.\n\nQuestions to Ask Before You Decide\n\n- Who handles the on-site work and coordination? Ask whether the contractor acts as the on-site lead or hands everything off. At HH Remodeling LLC, Abraham Becerra is the hands-on general and finish contractor who manages the crew for carpentry, drywall, tile, and paint while coordinating licensed plumbing and electrical trades.\n- How are permits and inspections handled? Moving fixtures or running new dedicated circuits triggers local building reviews. Ensure your contractor verifies local requirements and schedules rough-in inspections before closing walls.\n- What is the payment milestone structure? Look for payments tied to verifiable phases, such as completion of demolition, rough-ins, waterproofing, and final fixture trim.\n- How do you handle hidden water damage? Concealed subfloor rot or framing decay can halt progress. Confirm that your quote has a clear change-order process for structural repairs.\n\nClear communication from the start keeps your remodel on budget and on schedule. To discuss your Denver-area bathroom project with Abraham, call HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
